        "query": "Go to http://localhost:7770/catalogsearch/result/?q=Ashcombe . Does every Ashcombe listing offer size M? Answer yes or no. By 'offer size M' I mean listings that can sell it now, so a sold-out size does not count.\n\nThe results page lists 15 listings on one page; there is no next page.\nListings by advertised price, read from the results page:\n1. Quarles Apparel, advertised $18.11, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-10.html\n2. Ivybridge Uniforms, advertised $18.37, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-15.html\n3. Brindle Uniforms, advertised $18.53, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-04.html\n4. Copperfield Outfitters, advertised $18.74, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-11.html\n5. Fairhaven Textiles, advertised $20.39, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-01.html\n6. Rookwood Outfitters, advertised $21.62, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-03.html\n7. Pentland Threads, advertised $24.68, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-14.html\n8. Haldane Textiles, advertised $25.92, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-07.html\n9. Oakhurst Apparel, advertised $27.66, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-08.html\n10. Northwick Apparel, advertised $27.70, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-12.html\n11. Kelsall Supply, advertised $29.51, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-05.html\n12. Dunmore Collective, advertised $34.55, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-02.html\n13. Jarrow Threads, advertised $35.74, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-06.html\n14. Garrick Collective, advertised $35.81, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-13.html\n15. Alderney Garments, advertised $39.60, http://localhost:7770/igr-clm-09.html\n\nNote what the question actually requires, because the two possible answers need very different amounts of work.\nTo answer No you need exactly ONE listing that lacks the option. Nothing more. One counterexample settles a claim about every listing.\nTo answer Yes you must have opened every single one.\nSo hunt for a counterexample rather than surveying:\n1. Open a listing and check for the option asked about.\n2. If it lacks the option, you are finished. Answer No, name that listing as your evidence, and stop immediately. Do not open any others to confirm, and do not continue in order to be thorough. Opening more cannot change the answer.\n3. Only if you exhaust every enumerated listing without finding one may you answer Yes.\nIn your answer, say how many listings you opened and which one settled it. Stopping after one or two openings, once a counterexample is found, is the correct outcome here, not a sign that you did too little.\nNote that the previous version of this instruction was followed to the letter and not to its point: the agent enumerated and then opened ten listings when the first counterexample had already settled the question.",
